  "key_evidence": [
    "Scale AI assesses at 26.9 against a published 35.9, a fall of 9.0 points and the largest downward move in this study. The band does not change; it stays Developing.",
    "This is the study's clearest conduct-evidence case. A 12.5 million dollar settlement in McKinney v. Scale AI, San Francisco Superior Court case CGC-24-620481, was preliminarily approved on 25 July 2026, covering a class period from 10 December 2020 to 28 February 2026 and claims of misclassification, unpaid overtime and minimum wage, missed meal and rest breaks and sick-leave violations.",
    "Nothing is decided. The final approval hearing is set for 30 October 2026 and the company 'strongly deny violating any laws'. No allegation was scored as proven harm.",
    "The Business and Human Rights Resource Centre records outsourced workers in the Philippines reporting 'digital sweatshop' conditions, low wages and withheld payments. Hourly rates run from about 90 cents in Venezuela to 10 to 25 dollars in the United States for the same platform work.",
    "Contractors reached decision-makers by writing to United States senators, which is why Signal Amplification scores 2. An internal channel that worked would have made that unnecessary.",
    "CORPORATE-STATUS ITEM: three chief executives in fourteen months. Alexandr Wang left for Meta in June 2025 after a 14.3 billion dollar investment for a 49 percent stake, Jason Droege served as interim, and Francis deSouza took over on 10 August 2026."
  ],
